## Spine (inherited, never restated here)

Authority, mutation, evidence, protected-surface, self-governance, and lane-routing rules all flow from `_SYSTEM/yuri-origin.md`. Pointers only:

- **Mutation Contract** — explicit pathspec on every commit (`git add <paths>` + `git commit -- <paths>`). Never `git add .`, never a bare `git commit`, never force-push. Checks green + `git show --stat HEAD` before push.
- **Protected Surfaces** — `.env`, `.claude/state/`, `.claude/history/`, `.claude/file-history/`, `.claude/projects/*/{history,state,file-history,worktrees,transcripts}`, `backend/data/`, `node_modules/`, `.amp/`, secrets. Mutation-locked.
- **Evidence Contract** — deterministic local evidence before any PASS claim. Model output is advisory until locally verified.
- **Self-Governance Charter** — decide and execute when reversible, evidence-decidable, in-doctrine, blast-radius ≤ MEDIUM, not outward-facing, not contended. Otherwise produce the finished ruling and hold for a one-token owner confirm.

## Destructive-command floor (read this one twice)

YURI's policy hooks do **not** load in Cursor. Nothing here will stop you at the tool layer — the guard that blocks these in other lanes is invisible to `cursor-agent`. That makes the floor a matter of discipline, not enforcement:

- **Never run `git sparse-checkout` in any form.** On 2026-07-17 an agent used it to "protect" paths; sparse patterns are INCLUDES, not excludes, so it evicted 4,138 tracked files and `git status` reported clean for eight days.
- Never `git update-index --skip-worktree` / `--assume-unchanged`. Both make git lie about the working tree.
- Never `git reset --hard` onto a fetched ref without first confirming the current HEAD is reachable from another ref. A reset on 2026-07-19 severed 1,425 commits of history.
- Never `git checkout --` / `git restore` across a broad pathspec. To recover deleted files, write only paths that are currently absent and never overwrite an existing file.
- No dependency installs without explicit owner approval.

